blocks.en:
We prompt the VLM to produce a short product-title caption (8–15 words) describing the target item.
Three design principles, each grounded in encoder behavior:
(1) Product-title format : short captions avoid reference leakage and carry higher attribute density per token—we show in § 5 that attribute content, not linguistic style, is the primary mechanism behind CaptionFuse’s gains;
(2) No reference leakage : we forbid comparative language (“instead of,” “more than”) to prevent encoding reference attributes, which would pull the query toward the reference rather than the target;
(3) Attribute specificity : explicit instructions about color, material, style, pattern ensure the caption carries concrete visual attributes that the encoder can discriminate.

blocks.zh:
我们请 VLM 制作一个描述目标项目的短片标题( 8–15 字) 。
三个设计原则,每个都基于编码器行为:
(1) 产品标题格式:短标题避免参考漏洞,每个符号具有更高的属性密度——我们在§5中显示,属性内容而不是语言风格是CaptionFuse收益背后的主要机制;
(2) 不发生参考漏损:我们禁止比较语言(“而不是”“超过”)防止编码参考属性,因为编码属性会把查询引向参考而不是目标;
(3)属性特异性:关于颜色,材料,风格,图案的明晰指示,确保标题带有编码器可以区分的具体视觉属性.
